vals = []
for _, row in met.iterrows():
    numeric = {s: pd.to_numeric(row[s], errors='coerce') for s in samples}
    vals.append({sid: np.nanmean([v for k, v in numeric.items()
                                  if k.startswith(sid + '_')])
                 for sid in meta.id})
M = pd.DataFrame(vals, index=met.index).T
```

**Quantitative result**: 974 metabolite rows were represented across participant IDs; the analysis retained the 974 rows for testing (complete-case sample size was checked separately for each model).

