from scipy.spatial.distance import pdist,squareform
D=squareform(pdist(log.T,metric='euclidean'))
for a in order:
 z=D[np.ix_(labels==a,labels==a)]; print('within',a,z[np.triu_indices_from(z,1)].mean())
for i,a in enumerate(order):
 for b in order[i+1:]: print('between',a,b,D[np.ix_(labels==a,labels==b)].mean())
p=PCA(n_components=2).fit(log.T); print(p.explained_variance_ratio_)
```

**Quantitative result**: Within distances: AoSMC 207.568, fibroblast 234.657, melanocyte 232.338, SkMM 235.219. Between distances ranged 240.908 (fibroblast-SkMM) to 256.441 (AoSMC-fibroblast). PC1/PC2 explained 14.756%/2.553%.
